{
 "about": "Core Phosphene UI terms: what each IS, and the agreed word per language. Shared by the Studio and the Mac app tools. 'match' = English words, whole words (case-sensitive when written with a capital, so 'Outputs' the tab is not 'output codec') that count as this term. Per language: 'use' is the agreed word shown to translators; 'accept' lists the stems a translation must contain (any one) when the English uses the term. 'strict': true refuses a translation that drops the agreed word; otherwise it is a warning. A language with no entry gets the meaning only, and the translator proposes a word (python3 scripts/i18n_tool.py glossary <lang> lists them to fill in). One neutral file per language: no regional variants (zh-Hans for Chinese).",
